 { Most of the time, the right way to defend against pawn breaks is to stop them in their tracks! Find the best move for Black here. } 1... { -KEY- } h6 $11 { Correct! By stopping the h6 break Black keeps a healthy kingside structure. } ( 1... Rhf8 $2 { A careless move would leave Black on the back foot after } 2. h6 $1 g6 3. Rdf1 { Suddenly Black has no good way of saving the f6 pawn, since } f5 { runs into trouble after } 4. gxf5 gxf5 5. Rh5 $18 ) 

